                  </origin>
                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_66">Brecon, Brecknockshire.
                        Benedictine priory of St John the Evangelist</orgName><p>Hereford P.v.1
                        and Bodl. e Mus. 93 formed one volume, earlier probably at BATTLE, q.v. Sir
                        John Prise found it 'in Brechonia Demetarum . . . urbe . . . ex coenobio
                        Monachorum, quod ibidem erat Benedictini, quem vocant, ordine desumptum' (J.
                        Prise, Historiae Brytanniae Defensio, 1573, p. 114).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sir John Prise (d. 1555).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">e Mus. 93 belonged to Silas Taylor in 1658,
                     for whose dealings with Hereford library see Wood, Athenae, 3. 1175. It formed
                     part of the Hereford MS in s. xvi (see Cambridge, CCC MS 101, pp.
                     132--133).</provenance>
